# mutgap4_svc_complete_reads_listed_only: An exec's completion walks its resource list, count entries of {u32 reference, u32 flags}, and the first command buffer's {u64 VA, u64 length} follows the list: here that VA is 0x4_0000_0000 + X, read as a record it would name texture X with the synchronize flag (bit 2 of its high word). A depth-2 task of 0x100001 pages (16 GiB and a page) with a leaf at VA page 0x100000. A normal texture X (type 2, 4x4 RGBA8Unorm, blit-paged) is filled on the GPU by an exec that lists it with invalidateGuest only, so its host copy is newer; the guest writes 0xB7 over its pages. A second exec, whose command buffer is at 0x4_0000_0000 + X, lists only a shared buffer S with synchronize: nothing synchronizes X, and its pages keep the 0xB7. The same in every setup.
